 he  sees by the virtue of Good Friday turn  to Easter Sunday that the sufferings of  the Christian are actually used by God  to unite us even more perfectly to our  Lord and Savior the suffering one that  we may more perfectly share in the glory  of his resurrection coming from the  Apostle Paul this is no pious platitude  this is no empty conceit he is not being  naive he is not being insensitive this  is one who knows what it's like to  suffer he has seen the worst that our  world can offer and yet he rejoices and  now we as God's people we groan inwardly  yes but we groan with eager anticipation  the image here is of a young child  waiting at the Christmas tree days  before Christmas day eager to open his  presents he feels the angst of that  longing so near and yet so far they are  of course the analogy only works because  he expects that he will one day get to  open the presents and likewise we  Christians though we grow inwardly we  know that our hope is sure and that it  is not in vain and this steals us to  endure patiently this strengthens us to  endure to run the race that is set  before us not because the sufferings  that we continue to face don't vex us  not because they don't  hurt not because they don't frustrate us  not even because sometimes we do waver  in doubt but because we have seen in  Jesus Christ just how powerful God is to  turn our groanings into glory and so now  in this time of pandemic it is upon us  to be constant in our prayers now is the  time for us to be fervent in our hope  now is the time for us to be intentional  in our joy  let us sing praises to God in this  season I'm mindful of a friend of mine  out in Massachusetts right now a fellow  clergyman who as he looks out upon the  world all he can say is I must continue  constant in my daily prayers and tell  this plague passes and that is our  outlook that is the power of the  churches daily faithfulness that is the  power of God's people remaining constant  now is the time for us to commend  ourselves to God now is the time for us  to trust in him now is the time for us  to make good on our faith and to serve  our fellow brothers and sisters in the  Lord because none of the pain in this  world  none of the evil in this world not even  global pandemics can change this one  fact that Jesus Christ is raised that  Jesus Christ is glorified and as we have  hope in his kingdom come on earth on  this earth as it is in heaven  we have great assurance god be praised
 

